data.content:
The build errors are pre-existing in your test file (missing `using System;`). That's unrelated to hot reload setup. Here's what I did:

**1. Added the NuGet package:**
```
Microsoft.Testing.Extensions.HotReload (2.2.3)
```

**2. Created `Properties/launchSettings.json`** so `TESTINGPLATFORM_HOTRELOAD_ENABLED=1` is always set:

```json
{
  "profiles": {
    "TestProject": {
      "commandName": "Project",
      "environmentVariables": {
        "TESTINGPLATFORM_HOTRELOAD_ENABLED": "1"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

**Usage:** Run tests with `dotnet run --project .` (not `dotnet test`). The test host will stay alive and re-run tests automatically when you save code changes. Press Ctrl+C to stop.
